{
  "name": "Find work emails for new Google Sheets rows and add them to a campaign",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Find work emails for new Google Sheets rows and add them to a campaign\n\n### How it works\nTurn a spreadsheet of names and company websites into campaign contacts. When a row is added, the workflow checks that it has a first name, last name and domain, asks Argorant for the work email and adds people with a confirmed (valid) email to your campaign, with their name and company as variables. The status column says what happened: added, not confirmed, or no email found.\n\nCosts: 1 credit per email found, 0.25 when nothing is found. Rows that are incomplete cost nothing.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Prepare a sheet with the columns first_name, last_name, company, domain, email and status.\n4. Add a Google Sheets credential and pick the sheet in **New row** and **Write back the result**.\n5. Pick the campaign in **Add to campaign** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nLower the polling interval of **New row**, or add a column title and map it as the job title.",
        "height": 626,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "f0412108-bb01-4f6e-abd6-3abc1398221d",
      "name": "Overview",
